The Dockerfile generates instance_seed/sec.db deterministically from tracked
source data (PYTHONHASHSEED=0 python3 seed_data.py); the image build deletes
any instance_seed/ extracted from the pinned asset tarball and regenerates it,
asserting the frozen image-caliber sha256
59d95b8d5903063b0bbea21f38e57e31be4f06416d52cf397fa14f779e4d9e4b.
The tarball's instance_seed/sec.db copy (local dev caliber sha256
2d68d37888c2dc87cf4bd8766cc12a221966a64156ded693831e0f6de080e29e) is
therefore build-time dead weight, kept only for the pinned revision's
byte-integrity; scripts/fetch_assets.sh deletes it after extraction.
